@startuml uc005-design-sequence-no-verdicts
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-005 Generate report: design sequence (extension 1a: no case reached a verdict)

participant "cli.run_command()" as CLI
participant "scoring.summarise()" as Summarise
participant "summary:Summary" as Summary
participant "report.build_report()" as Build
participant "cli.print_summary()" as Print

note over CLI
  Every result is Outcome.ERROR, e.g. the target
  rejected the key: error_stage="target".
end note
CLI -> Summarise : summarise(results)
Summarise --> CLI : Summary(total=5, passed=0, failed=0, errors=5)
CLI -> Build : build_report(run, results, summary)
activate Build
Build -> Summary : evaluated
Summary --> Build : 0
Build -> Summary : pass_rate
Summary --> Build : None (evaluated is 0)
Build -> Summary : coverage
Summary --> Build : 0.0 (0 / 5)
Build -> Build : _case(result) for each: actual_answer, verdict,\ntarget_call, judge_call = None;\nerror = {"stage": "target", "message": ...}
Build --> CLI : report with "pass_rate": None,\nwhich json.dumps writes as null
deactivate Build
CLI -> CLI : write_report(...) as usual
CLI -> Print : print_summary(summary)
Print -> Summary : pass_rate
Summary --> Print : None
Print --> CLI : prints "Passed: 0  Failed: 0  Errors: 5  (of 5)"\nand "Pass rate: n/a (no case reached a verdict)"

note over Summary
  Business rule: an ERROR is never a FAIL.
  A null pass rate, not 0, says "nothing was judged" (AC-005-02).
end note
@enduml
